     wwssccoonnssccttll..ccoonnff — wsconsctl variables to set at system startup

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     wwssccoonnssccttll..ccoonnff contains a list of wsconsctl(8) variable assignments that
     is read at system startup by rc(8) during the boot sequence.

     The file is made up of wsconsctl(8) variable assignments (_v_a_r_i_a_b_l_e=_v_a_l_u_e)
     with comments designated by a hash mark (‘#’).

FFIILLEESS
     /etc/wsconsctl.conf
     /etc/examples/wsconsctl.conf

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     To load a Russian keyboard encoding, one would use the following line:

           keyboard.encoding=ru

     To set the screen burner timeout to 60 seconds, the following can be
     used:

           display.screen_off=60000

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     rc(8), wsconsctl(8)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     A wwssccoonnssccttll..ccoonnff file first appeared in OpenBSD 3.0.

